WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.360
Next, we have a speech from the 
new students' representative,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.720
Yotsuba Sayo.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.730
Yes, sir.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.120
She's so pretty!

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:29.910
She's hurt?

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.390
Climbing?

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.460
Yes. My dream is to participate 
in the world championships

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.270
and make climbing more popular everywhere.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.950
Nono!

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.450
You can do it!

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.950
Almost... there!

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.310
I made it!

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.960
Yay! I sent it for the first time!

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.960
You did it, Nono!

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:22.970
All right!

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.360
Sugiura sends the route!

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.980
<b>Kanto Bouldering Championship</b>

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:48.620
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.820
<b><i>Wall 5      Hard Work and Talent</i></b>

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.340
You know what?

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.430
I think I might bomb this competition.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:08.440
Huh...

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.180
Huh?!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.840
Nono-san?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:13.830
So...

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.430
If I do, we'll be counting on you.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.490
Wh-What are you saying?

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.610
You're a much better climber than me!

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:26.160
I'll be a complete non-factor 
in the team championship!

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.180
J-Just kidding!

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.690
Sorry.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.190
I guess I'm nervous.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.760
Did I scare you?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.190
Uchimura falls!

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.190
Grr!

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.320
What is with this slab?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.700
That last hold is way too far!

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.700
As the routesetter, what do you 
make of that fall, Nakada-san?

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.910
Hmm... I think she jumped a little early.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:56.440
You have to maintain your balance and 
place your foot on the volume to the left,

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.750
then raise your arms and perform a dyno.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.470
That's the perfect move sequence 
to solve this problem.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.350
Since I'm the one who set this problem,

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:08.000
I know that is the only 
sequence that can send it.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:16.730
<i>I should wait until I see someone 
else send this problem before I retry.</i>

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.410
Whoa, here comes one of the 
favorites to win this competition.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.610
We're about to see Fujita Masumi in action!

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:27.370
How will she tackle this problem, 
which no competitors have sent yet?

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.550
Fast! She's way too fast!

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.130
Fujita's moves are a blur! It's like we're 
watching a speed climbing competition!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.040
She's reached the zone hold 
in just a few seconds!

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.630
Will she finish things off here?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.840
<i>Hmph. Is she going to jump?</i>

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.520
<i>How hasty, my girl.</i>

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.520
<i>That is the wrong move to make.</i>

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.610
Get set!

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:05.900
What?!

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.730
She's got it!

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.440
Fujita Masumi has done it in one go!

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.760
Is it any surprise she's a favorite?

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:14.790
Hell yeah!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:19.210
What an incredible display of core 
strength and leaping ability!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.560
Amazing, Captain Masumin!

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.490
Killer!

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.950
Impressive, as always.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.220
Thank you, everyone.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.480
What the heck was that double dyno?

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.300
That's Fujita Masumi for you.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.220
Her climbing is characterized by her 
absurd explosiveness and vertical...

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:37.000
I'm going to try to send everything 
in my way. Follow my lead, girls.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:37.820
Yeah!

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.470
...which has given her the 
moniker of Black Panther.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.860
Dad, there are so many climbers.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.790
And they're all climbing at once.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:53.990
Yes. These prelims will decide the top 20,
 who will proceed to the semifinals.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.020
I don't really understand the rules.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.480
Competitive bouldering is a 
sport where climbers compete

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.000
over how many routes they can 
finish within the time limit.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.650
There are eight routes in total here.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:10.750
If two people send the same number, 
how are they ranked?

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.760
In that case, the next benchmark is

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.810
how many zones they've reached.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.910
Then, apart from sending, grabbing 
those bonus holds is important, too?

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.110
Verily!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:29.110
Dad, you seem to be enjoying yourself today.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.320
The rankings are determined by...

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:40.120
<b>Routes sent
↓</b>

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:40.210
<b>Zones reached
↓</b>

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:40.210
<b>Attempts needed
 to send routes
↓</b>

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:40.210
<b>Attempts needed
 to reach zones</b>

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.340
routes sent, zones reached,

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:40.210
attempts needed to send routes, 
and attempts needed to reach zones.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:46.090
Even if you fall, you can line up again 
and try each problem up to five times.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.590
But lining up again will eat up a lot of time.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.090
It does.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:56.600
How well you observe the field and use your 
time effectively is the key to victory.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.450
This problem involves a overhang.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:03.280
It seems pretty demanding. 
How will Kumagai climb this?

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.930
<i>There is only one thing I consider 
to be a major factor...</i>

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.990
<i>and that is strength!</i>

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.410
Wow! She's unbelievably strong!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.290
She's getting higher and higher 
using only her upper body!

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.550
<i>Isn't she going to use those edge holds?</i>

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.000
<i>That's the graceful way to climb!</i>

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.500
And sent! Talk about powerful climbing!

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.500
Give it up for the Muscle Maxima'am, 
Kumagai Chigusa!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.010
Strength is power!

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:37.510
<i>A gentle curve that rejects 
being trampled on.</i>

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:39.350
<i>But it is helpless before me.</i>

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.040
<i>Un,</i>

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:41.520
<i>deux,</i>

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.130
<i>relevé!</i>

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.020
<i>Un,</i>

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:46.520
<i>deux,</i>

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.140
<i>arabesque!</i>

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:53.160
Sent! Ooba mesmerizes with 
her exquisite balance!

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.720
That's our Ballerina of Rock.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.910
Believe it or not, ballet and climbing 
have a lot of common factors.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:03.040
Form, precise leg movements, 
and use of the hips to name a few.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:10.300
<i>To me, this problem was as 
basic as The Cupid Variation.</i>

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.580
<i>From what I can see, the pocket 
on top is pretty tricky.</i>

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.430
<i>It's likely that I won't be able to 
stabilize myself if I dyno to it,</i>

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:21.680
<i>so I should shift my body 
weight right, and...</i>

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.440
<i>Nice! Got it!</i>

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.690
Smooth! Yotsuba made good use 
of toeholds to secure the top hold!

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.340
The Princess of Lead does it again.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.200
Even in bouldering, her decision-making 
at altitude remains unmatched.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.700
We're seeing more and more 
climbers send routes in one go.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.640
Prelims or not, these problems 
are certainly not easy.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.960
It just goes to show the 
amount of talent we have here.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.130
<i>Where there is a will, there is a way. 
Just one more move to finish.</i>

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.090
<i>There!</i>

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.090
<i>I did...</i>

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:55.430
<i>it?</i>

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.590
<i>Why?!</i>

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.720
Whoa, Niijima?

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.840
It's not recognized as a send unless 
you get both hands on that hold.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.020
Darn.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.600
What are mew doing, Senpai?!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.700
<i>An incline with several sloper holds.</i>

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.300
<i>Judging by the people who went 
before me, the crux is...</i>

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.700
<i>the hold four hands up.</i>

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.880
Top climbers conquer walls twice.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:23.120
Once on sight, and once with their bodies.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:26.360
<i>Well, I've conquered it in mind already.</i>

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.120
<i>That leaves...</i>

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.810
Nobody has sent this problem yet.

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.130
The next one to attempt it is 
Hanamiya Girls' first-year,

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.630
Kasahara Konomi!

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:38.030
<i>Next up is the hold that 
dropped a bunch of people,</i>

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.600
<i>the blue sloper three hands up.</i>

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.100
<i>Okay, yeah, it's slippery!</i>

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.640
<i>I need to stabilize myself quickly!</i>

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:46.560
<i>Next,</i>

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.560
<i>I'll do a pied à main with my left leg,</i>

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.940
<i>and match the blue sloper.</i>

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.940
<i>Then, use the left heel hook to...</i>

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.070
Kasahara reaches the zone hold!

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:00.330
<i>Bless the shoes Asuka-san picked out for me.</i>

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.330
<i>They feel perfect!</i>

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:05.710
But going from here to 
the goal will be tough.

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:08.210
Some climbers reached the top hold,

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.960
but none of them could grab it 
and stabilize themselves.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:14.170
<i>Bad grips at this incline 
are a terrible combo.</i>

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:19.720
<i>It makes you want to close the distance 
to the top hold with a do-or-die dyno.</i>

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:26.060
<i>No, stay calm. Replay the sequence 
in your mind one more time.</i>

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.660
<i>Perform another pied à main 
with the left leg.</i>

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.100
<i>And then...</i>

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.460
Kasahara's matching that sloper?!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.690
<i>This hold is nothing!</i>

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:41.870
<i>Nothing compared to that crimper 
in the Anti-Monkey's second crux!</i>

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.370
<i>Keep both hands on the prize!</i>

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.830
Sent!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:49.640
Yes!

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.250
Sent in one! She becomes the 
first to send the problem!

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:57.710
<i>That means she solved that 
crux all on her own.</i>

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:02.010
<i>Can she one-shot any problem 
with enough time to observe?</i>

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:05.020
<i>She's a true on-sight climber.</i>

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:08.640
<i>She has wonderful analytic skills 
and climbs with practical precision.</i>

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.520
<i>Kasahara Konomi, just what is your deal?</i>

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.520
Master did it!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.780
Wow, Konomin. I can't 
believe you sent it in one.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:21.080
I thought Uehara-san was the only 
Hanamiya first-year to watch out for.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.530
I'll go through my data later, I'll have to!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.170
A powerful foe has shown up.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.840
And she's a first-year?

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:34.290
Oh? Interesting gal, 
that Kasahara Konomi-chan.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:39.550
Our next climber is Hanamiya Girls' 
second-year Sugiura Nono!

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.270
You can do it, Nono-san!

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:46.360
<i>Watching Konomin's one-shot 
gave me lots of confidence.</i>

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.900
<i>I'm gonna go all-out, okay?</i>

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.310
One, two...

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.850
three!

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.410
She's quickly pulling herself up high.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.280
Sugiura reaches the zone hold!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.200
<i>Okay, looking good.</i>

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.040
<i>Now...</i>

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:15.480
<i>I just need to corner this thing,
and I'll reach the top hold for sure!</i>

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.550
<i>Now for the left foot.</i>

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.510
<i>Okay!</i>

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.510
<i>Gotcha! The goal is right there.</i>

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:31.100
<i>I can't reach it?</i>

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.340
<i>But then, I can just...</i>

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:34.020
Nice!

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.020
A dropknee to a back-and-foot!

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:37.770
That should do it!

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:45.990
<i>Why can't I reach it? 
This should be the right sequence!</i>

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.800
<i>In the final problem of an 
important tournament last year,</i>

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:55.220
<i>I just couldn't grab the first hold 
and spent four whole minutes dynoing.</i>

00:12:55.220 --> 00:13:00.340
<i>I've spent the last half a year trying to 
make sure that would never happen again!</i>

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:04.720
Nono, please hang in there.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.100
Get there... get there...

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.470
Get there! Get there!

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.480
Get me there!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.480
Nono!

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:22.480
Oh no! Sugiura falls just one step away!

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:30.490
Why? Why can't I get to it?

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:39.000
Whoa! Here comes Iwamine Chinari, 
this competition's odds-on favorite!

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:45.260
She already has a finished 
route under her belt.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:48.200
How will she choose to attack this wall?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:14:00.020
Incredible! Her reach is every 
bit as long as it looks!

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:05.130
This problem's second hold needs 
to be tackled like Sugiura did it.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:07.530
It usually can't be reached without 
building up some momentum,

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:11.780
but Iwamine can reach it just 
by lifting her leg up a little.

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:14.080
Her climbing is misleading.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.990
It makes any problem look easy to solve!

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:20.790
The way she inches up the wall, 
even with her reach,

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:24.640
evokes the image of a spider 
approaching prey trapped in its web.

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:27.800
That's why she's the Climbing Spider, 
Iwamine Chinari!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:32.650
I see. So height is a real advantage 
in bouldering, isn't it?

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:35.610
No, that's a mistaken generalization.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:41.190
If anything, the longer your reach, 
the more your body sways in dynos,

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:45.850
and when holds are bunched up close, 
your body makes it hard to position yourself.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:50.160
<i>This is where things will start 
to get difficult for Iwamine.</i>

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.200
<i>How will she do this?</i>

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:55.950
<i>Ladies, let me get a good look</i>

00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:02.730
<i>at your adorable faces being 
struck with wonder and swooning.</i>

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:04.420
<i>What?!</i>

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:08.420
S-Sent! We have just witnessed 
the most audacious of moves!

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:13.560
I didn't set this problem 
to be solved with that crap!

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:17.160
She grabbed the top hold without 
even entering the corner!

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.560
Unbelievable reach!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.540
Unbelievable height!

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:24.750
No way. I couldn't reach 
it even with cornering...

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.230
Nono-san?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.440
Well, on to the next one.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.600
We haven't lost just yet.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:34.800
I'll definitely send the next one.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.160
Watch me, Konomin.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.840
R-Right.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.830
Okay, let's do this!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.370
As time goes on,

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:46.030
it becomes clear what the problems 
involve and how difficult they are.

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:50.460
The climbers need to identify 
which routes they can climb now.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.680
<i>I know this, I do.</i>

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:58.510
<i>This lemon-shaped volume is similar 
to a hold in the Rockaround Rock gym.</i>

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:02.360
<i>To improve my team's chances of victory,
 I ran around and collected</i>

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.400
<i>all kinds of climbing data,
 which is all stored in my brain!</i>

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.900
Satou finishes the route!

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.160
I did it, I did!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:14.360
Very nice. A beautiful climb, 
just as I envisioned.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:18.540
I shall show what the
 Lackey Data Climber can do, I daresay!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.120
<i>This sloper's slippery.</i>

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.040
<i>The top hold is right there...</i>

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:28.120
<i>The edge up next looks awkward, too.</i>

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.300
<i>What now?</i>

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:32.300
<i>You can't grab that edge 
with your fingers.</i>

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.850
<i>The top hold is right there!</i>

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:35.680
<i>My physical ability is top-notch.</i>

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.800
<i>Go for a do-or-die jump!</i>

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.310
<i>Don't take the easy way out,</i>

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:41.810
<i>Jun!</i>

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.190
<i>It's not great! But...</i>

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:49.740
<i>The crimps in outdoor rock faces 
have prepared me for this!</i>

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.450
Hell yeah!

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:57.450
Hanamiya's speedster, 
Uehara, sends the route!

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:02.270
Given her skills, one could say 
she's taking it slow and steady.

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:06.820
<i>Hear me, Caterno teammates.</i>

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.960
<i>Watch my ordinary-as-hell moves,</i>

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.210
<i>steal my techniques, and walk over my corpse.</i>

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:18.740
<i>I'm Samura Rina, Caterno's 
Crimson Stormtrooper.</i>

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.100
<i>My moves may be ordinary,</i>

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:23.070
<i>but I'm on fire when I climb!</i>

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:25.100
Samura finishes the route!

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:32.480
Her moves may be conservative, but her 
climbing is determined and passionate.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.690
Boss!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.130
You're the flamin' best!

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:38.990
Time is running out.

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:42.990
From here on, a single attempt could 
shake up the rankings in a big way.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:45.560
Why does this queue have such a long tail?

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.620
I don't have time for this!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.130
Oh no!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:54.510
Five, four, three, two, one...

00:17:54.510 --> 00:18:00.010
<b>Kanto Bouldering Championship</b>

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:59.290
With that, the girls' prelims 
are officially over!

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.510
Seven sends? Way to go, Captain!

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.960
Thank you.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:06.300
But you were way more impressive, 
Konomi-san.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.990
You finished four routes 
in your first appearance.

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:12.820
Oh, uh, I just managed to squeeze 
one more in right at the end.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.530
The top 20 qualify for the semis.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:18.240
You have a chance with four sends.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.200
I don't know...

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.200
The final results have been updated.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.210
<b>Rank</b>

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.210
<b>Name</b>

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.210
<b>#1 Iwamine Chinari</b>

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.210
<b>#2 Fujita Masumi</b>

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:31.210
The two climbers who sent every 
route finish first and second!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.960
I fell once.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.090
<b>#3 Kumagai Chigusa</b>

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.510
<b>#4  Yotsuba Sayo</b>

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.340
<b>#7 Samura Rina</b>

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.340
<b>#10  Uehara Jun</b>

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.230
Nicely done, Jun.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:40.470
Thank you.

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:42.750
I-I'm not on there...

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:46.220
Five sends and six zones, 
right? You're top 20, easy.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:49.450
<i>Now we get ranks 11-20.</i>

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.230
<i>The cutoff for the semis!</i>

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:54.230
Please, Satou Maruno... Satou Maruno!

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:56.730
Come on, come on.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.240
Rank 20? That means...

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.240
<b>#20   Kasahara Konomi</b>

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:05.740
Awesome, Konomi! All that training paid off!

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:09.620
I did it! It's my first time 
clearing prelims, it is!

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:13.130
You okay?

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:17.630
<b>#23  Sugiura Nonoka</b>

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.440
Nono-san!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.600
Give us a bit.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:36.570
They say short people have a disadvantage 
in bouldering, and they're not wrong,

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:41.350
but I feel like those prelim 
problems leaned into it too much.

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:46.200
Sheesh. It makes you want to slap 
the routesetter in the face, huh?

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.580
Sayo-chin.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:51.580
How many times have we 
competed at this venue now?

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.100
And each time you lose, you come here.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:59.560
You haven't changed at all since our 
first tournament together, Nono.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:01.970
You haven't changed at all, either.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:08.720
Whenever I'm down, you're with me
 and trying to cheer me up.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:11.770
Oh? I wasn't aware of that.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.770
Climbing?

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.430
My dream is...

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:19.780
Ever since that day, we've both 
given climbing our all together.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.820
And when we made it to high school, 
Hanamiya's Director,

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:28.920
your father, made it possible to 
get a club up and running at once.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:33.210
We've been climbing together,
 hoping to be the best in Japan someday.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.780
I couldn't have done it alone.

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:40.420
It's only because you're here 
that I've made it this far.

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:43.110
Thanks, Sayo-chin.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:44.740
But...

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.440
Deep down, I really...

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:53.430
Time and time again,
 I've felt that with my height,

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.590
I'm not cut out for bouldering.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:21:00.470
But complaining about that 
won't solve anything,

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.990
so I tried to never say it out loud.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:08.990
But today... after that competition...

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:14.950
Why did I have to be so tiny?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:20.750
I work so hard every day... 
I even drink so much milk!

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:22.260
Nono...

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:29.460
I hate this so much!

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:35.820
And Konomin did so well for us! 
I wanted to shine out there, too!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.190
It's okay. There's always next time.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:42.650
You can show everyone what 
you're capable of next time.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:58.430
Let's go.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:21:59.420
Yeah.

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b><i>Wall 6: Unbelievable?</i></b>
